OL,3,GNEWSADiary found in rubbish tip unlocks
OL,4,Asoldier's story
OL,5,
OL,6,FA diary found in a rubbish tip has
OL,7,Funcovered the story of an Australian
OL,8,FWorld War One soldier.
OL,10,FThe diary, discovered by a 12-year-old
OL,11,Fboy in 1965 in Stourbridge, had a
OL,12,Fbullet hole through it and was covered
OL,13,Fin blood. Its final entry was dated 10
OL,14,FAugust 1918 but little was known about
OL,15,Fthe soldier who had written it.
OL,17,FMore than a century later, former
OL,18,FDudley Museum curator, Colin Reid, set
OL,19,Fout to uncover his identity and
OL,20,Fdiscovered his links to the West
OL,21,FMidlands.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,353,350,200,160,0,100
